{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1551671-homebrew-celestial-ma-demonic-puppet-style","id":1551671,"title":"Homebrew Celestial MA: Demonic Puppet Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-13T21:51:43-07:00","id":1551671,"title":"Homebrew Celestial MA: Demonic Puppet Style","content":"Aloha! I homebrewed this for 1e. (the original notebook I wrote it in has long since been cast away, but I figured I'd take a stab at recreating it here for 3e. Any help or insight is appreciated.<br /> <br /> The Demonic Puppet Style was created by a Circle of Exalts known for their great love of the theater and notorious rivalries. These rivalries would eventually be their undoing as paranoia kept them apart when their advisers and underlings betrayed them. The style's original name of Mokurenken was lost to time, eventually becoming known as Demonic Puppet Style. A favorite of Assassins with awakened Essence as the tales of survivors allude to the idea of possessed dolls that move on their own and not armed warriors.<br /> <br /> The nature of this Art is to use one's performance and martial prowess to manipulate specially prepared dolls or puppets that mimic other skills through which an Exalt can channel essence for Charm effects. Wooden puppets can be made to excel in Archery while moving Armors can be made powerful Brawlers. Even Corpses can be manipulated to wield melee<br /> <br /> Armor: Demonic Puppet Style is compatible with Armor.<br /> <br /> Weapons: This style supports the use of Wires or strings which can be used as Garrotes to deal lethal damage as part of a Grapple gambit as well as specially prepared puppets or marionettes. These puppets are complex devices filled with clockwork or similar mechanisms to facilitate movement. Such puppets require complex manipulations through such wires which are used to direct their movement and animate them. Control wires are usually in place on the puppets, but affixing a wire is typically an action. Charms such as Whirlwind Armor Donning and Hauberk Summoning can explicitly be used to affix a number of wires equal to your Performance Skill as part of the Charm's activation.<br /> <br /> Unless modified with magic, the maximum distance these puppets can be operated is Yards equal to the Puppeteer's perform skill and each yard beyond the 1st reduces their Perform skill for the purposes of determining the maximum value of skills they can model.<br /> <br /> The maximum value of skills they can model is equal to the number of wires currently connecting puppet and puppeteer or the puppeteer's Performance skill, whichever is lower.<br /> <br /> By default, any puppet's attacks are made with Martial Arts. As a Demonic Puppeteer, the Style of the puppets is one of wild swinging and unnatural twists and bends of the body. The hand to hand techniques of the puppet master are positively anemic by comparison, with only injurious blocks and grabs with Iron Wire Reinforcement or Waiting Spider's Concentration. The full power of the style manifests when different kinds of puppets are applied as needed. A small gift given to a target can kill them in their sleep while you hide in a tree outside, a hulking contraption can lay siege to a tower while you hide behind the front line.<br /> <br /> Puppets of different materials and sizes have different costs and Physical Attribute maximums (TBD). Usually, you use your own Strength and Dexterity Attributes but a small puppet may have a Strength maximum below your own. Exceeding a Puppet's maximum causes one of its wires to come loose for each dot by which you exceed the maximum. <br /> So if a small Paper Puppet has a Strength Max of 1, and you use your Strength of 5 when dealing damage, 4 of its control wires will come loose. If the puppet is within arm's reach, you can use Whirlwind Armor Donning to affix Wires as described above as a specific exception to its normal application.<br /> <br /> Charms (this is just the gist for now. As I get a better handle on the general mechanics I'll try to continue updating them).<br /> <br /> Invisible Thread Manipulation<br /> Essence 1/MA 1 and Performance 2<br /> Supplemental<br /> 1 or 3m. Lasts a Scene<br /> This charm has 3 functions. First, it allows the Puppeteer to effectively model a puppet's skills a their full rating out to a distance of Essence x 5 Yards. Second, it renders any strings or wires used to manipulate puppets nigh invisible and frustratingly difficult to cut. A creature attempting to attack such strings must succeed on an Awareness roll at a difficulty of the puppeteers Essence or 3, whichever is higher. The difficulty to attack such strings is equal to the Puppeteer's evasion + their Performance skill. The roll to perceive them must occur on the same Tic as the attack or the string becomes invisible again. Alternatively, for 1 mote this charm can be activated to affix 1 control wire to a puppet suitable for use with this style immediately before an attack is made with it.<br /> <br /> Iron Wire Reinforcement<br /> Essence 1/MA 1 and Performance 2<br /> Reflexive<br /> Prereq: Invisible Thread Manipulation<br /> 1 or 5m Instant or Scene<br /> For 1m activating this charm when a string is hit grants it a Hardness of 10 and Attackers making bare-handed attacks blocked with such wires suffer 1L damage unless a 2 die or better stunt was used to attack. For 5 motes the effect lasts a Scene and such wires can be used to enhance crushing attacks made during a Grapple Gambit allowing them to deal lethal damage. At Essence 3 such lethal attacks penetrate armor.<br /> <br /> Waiting Spider's Concentration<br /> Essence 1/MA and Performance 2<br /> Simple<br /> Prereq: Iron Wire Reinforcement<br /> 3 or 8m Scene or until triggered<br /> By activating this charm the Martial Artist's sense of touch is heightened and extended through the wires connecting them to the puppet. The vibrations produced by sounds within Essence x 5 yards of the puppet are conducted back to the puppeteer's waiting fingers and interpreted as readily as visual information. A martial artist using this Charm can instead use it to spread wires around themselves. While these wires are spread the martial artist becomes aware of any creature or effect within its radius of Essence x 5 yards not actively trying to conceal itself. Whenever the martial artist senses such a creature they can make reflexive attack or Grapple gambit using the wires as a medium weapon that deal lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Blue Fairy's Blessing<br /> Prerequisites: Iron Wire Reinforcement, Special<br /> When wielding Puppets with this Martial Art the Exalt can channel any Athletics charms they know through the puppet, using its Attribute values or their own where relevant.<br /> This charm can be repurchased multiple times, each time it's purchased it grants another one of the following options (provided the listed prerequisites are met) that permanently upgrade the Demonic Puppeteer's capabilities.<br /> <br /> Wooden Stooges<br /> The puppeteer can draw out the secret aptitudes of Wood. You treat the Attribute maximums of all Wooden Puppets as 1 higher. The character can make Archery or Thrown Attacks with the puppet. If the character knows Archery or Thrown charms and the puppet meets the skill prerequisites to use them (based on the Martial Artist's Performance skill, number of connected wires, and distance from the puppet), the character can use those charms to enhance its attacks. Alternatively, the Puppeteer can purchase those charms at 1/2 cost and treat them as Evocations unique to their puppets.<br /> <br /> Cavorting Corpses<br /> Prereq: Medicine 2<br /> The puppeteer can manipulate Corpses. A Corpse's Attribute maximum is the same as the creature when it was living. This grim art typically allows the puppeteer to manipulate those familiar with the cadaver's former occupant. If the character knows Socialize or Presence charms and puppet meets the skill prerequisites to use them (based on the Martial Artist's Performance skill, number of connected wires, and distance from the puppet), the character can use those charms to enhance its social attacks.<br /> Note: at the ST's discretion, attempting to use this on an incapacitated living target might be possible, but if they aren't comatose or drugged into slumber, but as soon as they awaken, they can end the effect by tearing free of the threads suffering 1L.<br /> <br /> Ambling Armors<br /> Prereq: Resistance 2 or Craft (Metals) 2<br /> The Puppeteer can fashion powerful puppets out of steel and other metals. You treat the Attribute maximums of all Armored Puppets as 1 higher. The character can make Melee and Brawl Attacks with the puppet. If the character knows Melee or Brawl charms and the puppet meets the skill prerequisites to use them (based on the Martial Artist's Performance skill, number of connected wires, and distance from the puppet), the character can use those charms to enhance its attacks. Alternatively, the Puppeteer can purchase those charms at 1/2 cost and treat them as Evocations unique to their puppets.<br /> <br /> Paper Pawns<br /> The least expensive minions to replace, and some might consider the most cruel in combat. You treat the Attribute maximums of all Paper Puppets as 1 higher. Your paper puppet's unarmed attacks are Aggravated. If the character knows Stealth or Linguistics charms and the puppet meets the skill prerequisites to use them (based on the Martial Artist's Performance skill, number of connected wires, and distance from the puppet), the character can use those charms to enhance its such. Alternatively, the Puppeteer can purchase those charms at 1/2 cost and treat them as Evocations unique to their puppets.<br /> <br /> Demonic Puppet Form<br /> By sinking into a trance the Demonic Puppeteer all but abandons her body. Her deft movements and essence allow her to push her puppet minions to the very limits of their capability by quickly reattaching control threads. You increase the Physical Attributes and minimums of your active Puppets by 1. You can artificially improve your Puppet's dice pool by sacrificing Control wires after an action resolves, essentially wrenching with such force the puppet exceeds its limits and your own. Each wire sacrificed becomes an additional dot in either Strength or Dexterity, you decide which for each Wire lost, the additional dice for this improvement are non-Charm dice. At the end of your turn you may reflexively reattach 1 control Wire to a Puppet you are currently controlling.<br /> <br /> Wicker Man's Dance<br /> 3a Simple<br /> You shunt your bonfire or Iconic Anima to the puppet causing it to explode in a raucous and destructive manner.<br /> <br /> Marching Marionette Parade<br /> You can manipulate up to Essence Puppets at once, but must divide your Control wires between all active puppets. You can typically only cause 1 Puppet to act per turn, but can flurry their actions, sacrificing control wires as Part of Demonic Puppet Form also reduces flurry penalties.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral Thread Weaving<br /> Essence 3<br /> 10m 1wp Scene<br /> Activating this charm immediately affixes Essence Wires to a target. You no longer need to use physical Wires. These function as if you'd used Invisible Thread Manipulation and Iron Wire Reinforcement and can only be attacked with Spirit Cutting Attack or similar magic.<br /> <br /> Shadow Soul Puppeteer<br /> Essence 4<br /> You can use your Ephemeral Thread Weaving to try and puppet a living person. They can break Essence Wires each round automatically, but any time you have 5 wires on them you can force them to use Charms they know.<br /> <br /> \u200bStrider's Absent Master<br /> Essence 5 Seize control of a Warstrider. Automatic success on unoccupied or defunct Strider, vs control of pilot if occupied and pilot isn't incapped.<br /> <br /> Material Resource Costs (cumulative with Size)<br /> Paper o<br /> Wood oo<br /> Armor ooo<br /> Corpse - or ooo (just any corpse is pretty easy, but a specific corpse is likely wanted elsewhere)<br /> <br /> Small o<br /> Medium oo<br /> Large oooo<br /> <br /> Material Str Max (cumulative w/ Size)<br /> Paper o<br /> Wood ooo<br /> Armor oooo<br /> <br /> Size Str Max <br /> Small -<br /> Medium o<br /> Large ooo<br /> <br /> Material Dexterity Max (cumulative w/ Size Max)<br /> Paper oooo<br /> Wood ooo<br /> Armor oo<br /> <br /> Size Dex Max<br /> Small ooo<br /> Medium oo<br /> Large o","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28845-matt_c","name":"Matt_C","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T03:47:00-07:00","id":1552098,"title":"","content":"You should probably check out Exigents: Out of the Ashes if you've not already. There's some overlap with Pakpao the Puppeteer that might prove informative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}